{
  "case_id": "2018-17-340",
  "document_hash": "c88990bdd34e2ee2e18759f503279433b31e0f8c314e2f741b1d59d2fc4629fa",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "New Prime Inc.",
      "case_id": "2018-17-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c88990bdd34e2ee2e18759f503279433b31e0f8c314e2f741b1d59d2fc4629fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c88990bdd34e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The First Circuit held that independent contractor agreements are contracts of employment and, therefore, they were exempt from the Federal Arbitration Act. This reading of Section 1's exemption is contrary to the plain meaning of the statute and its structure, purpose, history, and context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c88990bdd34e2ee2e18759f503279433b31e0f8c314e2f741b1d59d2fc4629fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c88990bdd34e-0000-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The First Circuit held that independent contractor agreements are contracts of employment and, therefore, they were exempt from the Federal Arbitration Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c88990bdd34e2ee2e18759f503279433b31e0f8c314e2f741b1d59d2fc4629fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c88990bdd34e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How about the word \"work\" -- \"worker\" in the very clause? Shall apply to contracts of employment of seamen, railroad employees, or any other class of workers engaged in foreign or interstate commerce."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "New Prime Inc.",
      "case_id": "2018-17-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c88990bdd34e2ee2e18759f503279433b31e0f8c314e2f741b1d59d2fc4629fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c88990bdd34e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the Section 1 exemption, Congress did not define or suggest it was coming up with a new, creative interpretation of the word \"employment\" or \"employees,\" which was also used in that clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "New Prime Inc.",
      "case_id": "2018-17-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c88990bdd34e2ee2e18759f503279433b31e0f8c314e2f741b1d59d2fc4629fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c88990bdd34e-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If Mr. Oliveira is correct, he'd be entitled to further relief under the Fair Labor Standards Act, which is one of the provisions he's suing under."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c88990bdd34e2ee2e18759f503279433b31e0f8c314e2f741b1d59d2fc4629fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c88990bdd34e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Is there any other area of law where we take the party's label, \"employee\" versus \"independent contractor,\" and give it binding effect? I -- I -- I thought, for virtually every other purpose in tax law, labor law -- I -- I just don't know another area where we take the form of the contract as dispositive of a legal issue, of whether you're an employee or an independent contractor?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c88990bdd34e2ee2e18759f503279433b31e0f8c314e2f741b1d59d2fc4629fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c88990bdd34e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: May I -- may I go back to Justice Alito's question --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c88990bdd34e2ee2e18759f503279433b31e0f8c314e2f741b1d59d2fc4629fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c88990bdd34e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: It sort of sounds like what you're saying is that if the person is a real independent contractor, then the person is outside of -- is -- is outside of the exemption, but if the -- if the entity is not a real independent contractor, which is your argument here regarding Mr. Oliveira, it's different."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Prime",
      "case_id": "2018-17-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c88990bdd34e2ee2e18759f503279433b31e0f8c314e2f741b1d59d2fc4629fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c88990bdd34e-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I want to quickly address one point that Prime said. Prime -- Prime says that none of the sources that we have cited are in the context of distinguishing between independent contractors and common law servants. And that's, in fact, not true."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c88990bdd34e2ee2e18759f503279433b31e0f8c314e2f741b1d59d2fc4629fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c88990bdd34e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Suppose you win on the issue of arbitrability, the court says \"I'm going to decide whether the exemption applies,\" but then you lose on the issue of the interpretation of the exemption, the court says \"it doesn't apply to an independent contractor, Mr. Oliveira's an independent contractor; therefore, I'm going to order arbitration.\" Would the arbitrator then be bound by the determination that he is an independent contractor for purposes of applying the Fair Labor Standards Act?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2018-17-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c88990bdd34e2ee2e18759f503279433b31e0f8c314e2f741b1d59d2fc4629fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c88990bdd34e-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Was it Coppage v. Kansas, shall not join a union? Was that the contract at issue?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Boutrous",
      "case_id": "2018-17-340",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c88990bdd34e2ee2e18759f503279433b31e0f8c314e2f741b1d59d2fc4629fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c88990bdd34e-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We cite Black's Law Dictionary, which says, \"A contract of employment,\" and this -- tracking it back to 1927 -- \"was an agreement between an employer and an employee that states the terms and conditions of employment.\""
    },
